{
 "id": "thm-a1-curve-upper",
 "blueprint": {
  "is": "thm-a1-curve-upper",
  "from": null,
  "same_as": []
 },
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Compact-support upper bound on a curve",
 "statement": "Let $C_0$ be a smooth geometrically connected curve and let\n$\\mathcal F$ be a lisse Weil sheaf that is punctually $\\iota$-pure of\nweight $w$. Then every $H_c^r(C,\\mathcal F)$ has weights at most\n$w+r$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-general/sk-l-dl-general-open-line/thm-a1-curve-upper.md",
  "place": "node thm-a1-curve-upper, order 2828"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-weil-ordinary-compact-cohomology",
  "def-weil-punctual-weights",
  "d-real-setup",
  "def-pod-lisse-l-adic-sheaves",
  "def-weil-weil-sheaf-complex",
  "def-weil-frobenius-module-weights"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Put $U_0=C_0$ and $j=\\operatorname{id}_{C_0}$. Its image is the whole curve, so it is a dense open immersion and both its source and target are the given smooth geometrically connected curve. The middle extension of [def-wf-middle-extension] is ordinary $j_*\\mathcal F$, not $Rj_*\\mathcal F$. For the identity map, ordinary direct image evaluates $\\mathcal F$ on the same site objects with the same restrictions, hence $j_*\\mathcal F=\\mathcal F$; the induced Weil structure is the same Frobenius isomorphism. Thus this equality is an equality of Weil sheaves, not just an identification after forgetting Frobenius.",
   "uses": [
    "def-wf-middle-extension"
   ],
   "elementary": true,
   "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-general/sk-l-dl-general-open-line/thm-a1-curve-upper.proof.md",
    "place": "Proof: identity open immersion and its middle extension"
   }
  },
  {
   "text": "Apply [prop-a1-middle-extension-curve-upper] to this dense open immersion and the original lisse sheaf $\\mathcal F$. The source and target are smooth and geometrically connected, and punctual $\\iota$-purity of weight $w$ is exactly the hypothesis already given. For every degree $r$ it gives weights at most $w+r$ on $H_c^r(C,j_*\\mathcal F)$. Substituting the identity middle extension from step 1 makes this the asserted bound on $H_c^r(C,\\mathcal F)$, with its same Frobenius action. No affineness, properness, ramification condition, irreducibility or nonzero-rank assumption is used.",
   "uses": [
    "prop-a1-middle-extension-curve-upper"
   ],
   "elementary": false,
   "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-general/sk-l-dl-general-open-line/thm-a1-curve-upper.proof.md",
    "place": "Proof: identity open immersion and its middle extension"
   }
  }
 ],
